WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.220
- Hey legal eagles, one of the questions

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.357
I get most from college students is,

00:00:04.357 --> 00:00:07.612
"What is the best
undergrad degree or major

00:00:07.612 --> 00:00:10.050
"to prepare you for law school?"

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.520
Well today I'm gonna talk
about the various pros and cons

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.720
of different degrees and
by the end of this video

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.570
you will know what is
the right major for you.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.063
So stick around.

00:00:19.063 --> 00:00:21.646
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.000
The thing about law
school is that it takes

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.720
a lot of different skills

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.120
working in conjunction with each other.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.820
First and foremost, you
have to be a great writer.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.210
Second, you have to be
good at researching.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.750
You have to be good at logical thinking.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.970
You have to be able to
make good policy arguments

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.300
stemming from philosophy and government.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.930
You have to be good at
historical precedent.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.239
You have to be a good orator.

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:51.070
All of these things need
to work in conjunction

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.970
if you're going to get
the most out of law school

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.810
and you have to use all
of these skills together

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:59.170
in order to be a successful law student.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.640
To get good grades.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.740
And as a result there is no one major

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.320
that prepares you for law school.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.860
Law school is unlike anything else.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.260
In undergrad, in high school,

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.140
there is just simply nothing like it.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.840
And there is no one major
that really prepares you

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.010
for what law school is like.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.310
Final exams in law school are based on

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.760
what's called an issue
spotter hypothetical

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.210
where you're required
to think like a lawyer.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:29.830
No undergrad major prepares
you for thinking like a lawyer.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:32.200
In fact, law school
doesn't even prepare you

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.370
for thinking like a lawyer either.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.760
That's why we created a masterclass

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.260
to actually teach students

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.000
how to think like a lawyer.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.720
And classes in law school are taught

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.450
using the Socratic method

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.150
which is also completely different

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:48.310
from almost any seminar
or lecture that you've had

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.600
in college or in high school.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.150
Professors pepper their
students with questions

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.996
to reveal the right answer.

00:01:55.996 --> 00:01:58.560
Much in the same way that it's said

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.300
that Socrates peppered his disciples,

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.510
Plato and Aristotle with questions

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.780
to let them find the right answer.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.390
But this methodology, it's totally unlike

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.610
anything that you'll see in college.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.990
Especially where you have large classes

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.840
of hundreds of people or more

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:16.460
where there just simply isn't the ability

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:20.020
to go back and forth between
any particular student.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:21.890
And the subject matter in law school

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:25.900
is also totally different
from any undergrad subject.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.380
No one will teach you
the law that you need

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.020
before you get to law school.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.670
Sure, you might take a business law class

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.600
or an accounting law class

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.095
but that is such a small, tiny percentage

00:02:38.095 --> 00:02:40.300
of what you're going
to cover in law school

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.180
that there's no way for
any particular major

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.430
to really lay the foundation

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.920
of what you will need
to know in law school.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:48.990
So the question is this.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.980
If no major really
prepares you for law school

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.480
and no major can prepare
you for law school,

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.110
what major should you
sign up for in college

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.890
to best prepare you for law school?

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:05.180
Well the answer that
I always give is this.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.778
You should sign up for the major

00:03:06.778 --> 00:03:10.000
that you are most interested in.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.680
Get a degree in a subject
that you find fascinating.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.530
Law schools don't care about your major.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.357
When you apply to law school,
no law school is gonna look at

00:03:20.357 --> 00:03:23.160
which particular major you had.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:27.010
But they do care about what
grades you got in college

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.450
or in undergrad.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:29.700
So if you major in something

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.580
that you're really interested in

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.430
you are much more likely
to put more effort into it

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.310
and to do well in college.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.930
And that will translate
into better grades.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.850
Not to mention you will have
spent four to five years

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:44.970
studying something that you really enjoy

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.528
because you're never going
to get that time back.

00:03:47.528 --> 00:03:51.110
Odds are you're probably
going to enjoy law school less

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:52.900
than your time in college.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.873
So you might as well enjoy the most

00:03:54.873 --> 00:03:57.070
out of your college experience.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.750
So sign up for a major, get a degree

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.970
in something that you find fascinating

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.140
and you're willing to
study for four years.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.850
Then when you show up for
your first day of law school

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.530
you'll be in basically the
same boat as everybody else.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.210
You'll be starting from zero.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.740
Because no one's major or
degree actually prepared them

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:16.610
for law school.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.990
So it's okay that you're
starting from the same point

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.200
as everybody else.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.020
So what is the best major for you?

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:25.610
Well, that depends.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.530
It depends on your personal preferences.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.400
What do you enjoy studying?

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.180
What are you fascinated by?

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:36.108
What can you see yourself
studying for four to five years?

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:38.920
And what can you reasonably do

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:42.240
to get good grades in
that particular major?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.940
So unfortunately, I can't
give you one particular answer

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.300
that works for everybody.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.070
There is no one major that
works for all law schools

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.570
and even pre-law majors
don't really prepare you

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:54.723
for law school.

00:04:54.723 --> 00:04:56.860
For those of you who are unsatisfied

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:58.980
with an it depends answer,

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.170
well I'm sorry to say

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.270
that you're gonna have to get used to it

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.290
because if you're going to become a lawyer

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.480
you're going to hear it depends a lot.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.060
If you ask a lawyer anything,

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:11.120
nine times out of 10 you'll
get the answer that it depends.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.000
So let me know.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.640
What major did you sign up for?

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.440
What are you going to study in college

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.730
and what have you been studying?

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.770
Do you feel like it was
a good use of your time

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:20.940
for four years?

